{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Semiring","symbolKind":"protocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Semiring"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Semirings\/Semiring.swift#L31","fileName":"Semiring.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Semirings"}],"externalID":"s:9Semirings8SemiringP","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Semiring","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"A semiring (S, ⊕, ⊗, 0̄, 1̄), the algebra of path problems (Mohri 2002; Gondran–Minoux 2008).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Semiring"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Equatable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ extends a path by an edge and ⊕ combines alternative paths. The shortest-path entry points in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPaths answer a different question for each conformer. The tropical semiring gives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, the bottleneck semiring widest paths, the Boolean semiring reachability, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting semiring the number of paths.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A conformer implements the four requirements. The type system does not check the laws, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm’s result is meaningful only when they hold:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊕ is associative and commutative, with identity "},{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ is associative, with identity ","type":"text"},{"code":"one","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"text":" annihilates: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊗ 0̄ == 0̄ ⊗ a == 0̄"},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ distributes over ⊕ from both sides."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ need not be commutative. Algorithms always compute ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distance ⊗ weight"},{"text":", in path order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdditiveArithmetic.zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No semiring type here is a number, and a tropical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is +∞.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operators ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊕"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊗"},{"text":" call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plus(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"times(_:)"},{"text":", so the two spellings always agree.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Prefer the methods where another module might declare the same operators, and inside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"text":". That macro folds an expression without these operators’ precedences, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a ⊕ b == c)"},{"text":" does not type-check, while ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a.plus(b) == c)"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ"],"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From"},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring"],"type":"inheritedBy","title":"Inherited By"},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BooleanSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BottleneckSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/CountingSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/MaxPlusSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/TropicalSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/ViterbiSemiring"],"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/semiring"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-2ou28","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-93rtg"],"generated":true,"title":"Operators","anchor":"Operators"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/plus(_:)","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/times(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/one","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/zero"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings/Semiring/zero":{"abstract":[{"text":"0̄: the identity 